Consider the following C function:

```c
int f(int x, int y) {
    for (int i = 0; i < y; i++) {
        x = x + x + y;
    }
    return x;
}
```

Which of the following statements about the function is/are true?

Consider the following code using `fork()` and `wait()`. Assume the code compiles and runs correctly, and all system calls succeed:

```c
int x = 3;
while (x > 0) {
    fork();
    printf("hello");
    wait(NULL);
    x--;
}
```

How many times is `printf` executed in total?
